{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie","id":1401635,"title":"[D20] How to use Lupines as a threat but not entirely wipe the coterie?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-08T00:21:01-07:00","id":1401635,"title":"[D20] How to use Lupines as a threat but not entirely wipe the coterie?","content":"So... I'm running a D20 game (and if you're in that one - you know who you are - stop reading here), and recently the coterie killed a bunch of kinfolk. They really didn't have another choice, so I don't wanna hold it too harshly against them.<br /> <br /> They're currently not in a city, can't go to one either. Some of the kinfolk had found them and realized what they are, and were about to find a werewolf pack to tell on them. There was little the coterie could do to stop them except wiping them out.<br /> They have maybe 10-15 armed soldiers with them - 5 of them ghouls, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Now if a pack of werewolves were to find the remains of their kinfolk, they'll be surely pissed. They'll start to track down the killers and will eventually find the coterie (again they can't move - they're here on Sire's orders).<br /> <br /> Now if they're smart, they wait for a sunny day, rush in start murdering the guards (none of which have silvered weapons so its gonna be a massacre). Even if one of the kindred wakes from the noise, they can't actually do anything since they'd have to enter sunlight. Then they just tear their shelter to shreds and watch them burn.<br /> <br /> Obviously that would be a somewhat disappointing end to the coterie and the game.<br /> <br /> The big problem is that the Coterie doesn't know when and even if at all the attack is gonna happen. It's likely gonna be weeks or even months after the killing of the kinfolk. The pack just doesn't come by that often. And I doubt the werewolves would post a notice &quot;Tomorrow at midnight you'll die. - Sincerely the local werewolf pack&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of the vampires (there's three total) made sure to have his weapon silvered and he's generally a combat monster, so I wouldn't be surprised if he can actually one-shot a lupine (at least a young one). The other two... less so.<br /> <br /> So, i'm currently looking for ways how to make this work, use them as a threat in the future, without it just being a combat encounter, or a TPK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T01:46:32-07:00","id":1401640,"title":"","content":"Are they sitting where the kinfolk where killed, or are they a little distance away. IF the latter, then lots of wolf howling in the night from that direction would give them some warning, and allow for a hasty defence.<br /> <br /> Also they have troops with them - how well trained, and are they able to drill and so forth? Also are they generally building defences - troops need something to keep them occupied/busy, and fortify the position, clearing sight lines and so forth are good tasks - and ones the troops can see themselves beniifitting from.<br /> <br /> Also I'd go with a small (possible 3 wolf) pack, so there is a hope of dealing with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T02:19:34-07:00","id":1401641,"title":"","content":"when the lupines attack, have an NPC (or NPCs) attack the lupines out of nowhere, maybe kill a few of them and distract the others long enough to let the coterie escape or something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T02:22:28-07:00","id":1401642,"title":"","content":"Eh, the coterie slaughtered a family out of hand because they slipped up and decided to take the easy way out. I say they made their bed let them lie in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T03:55:14-07:00","id":1401653,"title":"","content":"I agree with Damian. By a whole family of Kinfolk the only way to survive would be run ASAP into a large city and pray the Prince use not them to sacrifice as a peace offer. The only other altivernative if they would have good luck during bad that the area whas only to take care of a lone garou.<br /> <br /> An other alternative would be, that the Kinfolk would be of the BSD, now it is the BSD while another Garou group is on the hunt of them.<br /> But yeah in most cases the coterie is fucked because the garou do not like those that slaugther their family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:09:51-07:00","id":1401681,"title":"","content":"First of all I believe that there's always a choice so they didn't have to kill them. During my games those characters would end dead (especially if they have Humanity below 7, which means they smell Wyrm).<br /> BUT<br /> <br /> It's your game so I will try to help you with that. I will give you four options, ordered by propability.<br /> <br /> 1. You could have the pack going after a bigger threat so they won't go after the coterie ASAP. From now on the coterie should shiver everytime they hear a howling. <br /> 2. The garou will let them live if they will turn their over Sire(s) AND at least one Kindred for every Kinfolk they killed (or for any of them). That means everything: location, defenses etc. Of course they could send the pack aftert a Cainite so powerful that he will easily defeat the Garou. BUT he can also take one prisoner and find out characters betrayal. And the pack could also go after the coterie when they will deal with their friends. They are traitors and creatures of the Wyrm. In this option the best tribes are the ones who don't mind get their hands dirty p. ex. Uktena.<br /> 3. The leader (or the entire pack) is very fond of challenges. They are also very honourable. I would make them Fianna or Get of Fenris. The leader decides to challenge one of them (or all of them if you want) for a fight to death. If the Cainite wins they will go unmolested. And let the dice roll (either figuratively or literally). Or they could attack at night cause slaying an unarmed sleeping enemy would be dishonourable.<br /> 4. Let the Garou (this time I think Children of Gaia would be the best) attack. When they will be on the coterie heads a gurahl (werebear) show up. He gives the Garou a choice: he will put his life on the line if they let the coterie walks away (this will work especially when at least one of the Cainites was Embraced by force). Gurahl knows a Ritual which can revive the dead but could also ends his life (more details in Gurahl sourcebook or old Werewolf Players Guide).<br /> <br /> Also remember that ordinary bullets (especially from automatic weapons) could stop werewolf as quickly as silver ones. You just have to fire more of them. So the guards could be a factory.<br /> <br /> And remember also about Garou nature:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/tacimur/art/WTA-awkwardness-260889602\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/tacimur/a...ness-260889602</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-08-2020, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T11:04:18-07:00","id":1401715,"title":"","content":"If the Garou don't know that these kinfolk are dead, and may not learn until months later, how exactly will they track down their killers? Scent doesn't last that long. And even most supernatural powers won't help you. How will they be able to determine it was the PCs who did this?<br /> <br /> Is it possible that the Garou find the dead kinfolk, get upset, and are not able to do anything about it? If so, they might turn the countryside into very hostile territory, but not lash at at vampires or at least specifically at these vampires. From a Garou perspective, maybe it was fomori who killed them, or normal human bandits, or wild animals, or something else.<br /> <br /> And unless this group of kinfolk are specifically related to this Garou pack, they'll likely be limits to their vengeance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T11:23:06-07:00","id":1401721,"title":"","content":"They killed an ENTIRE family of Kinfolk? Nope, that coterie is bye-bye if you want be realistic about it. It's not going to be just the &quot;pack,&quot; but probably the entire sept of the area is going to be tracking down the Vampires. Kinfolk are VERY important to ALL the Fera breeds- not only are they the missive to gain more potential Fera, they are the close families of the Fera itself- probably being some of the Kinfolk being their own father or mom probably. Their going to be tracked to Oblivion and back no matter what. You can string it along with that the Garou haven't found the coterie yet, but when they do, its game over if they fail the ensuing combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T11:51:33-07:00","id":1401725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401715#post1401715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Garou don't know that these kinfolk are dead, and may not learn until months later, how exactly will they track down their killers?</div> </div> </div> </div>OP said &quot;they can't move - they're here on Sire's orders&quot;, and they're outside the city,<br /> meaning this coterie is probably the first vampires those garou are gonna meet, and this won't end well for the coterie, even if the garou don't know they're the killers,<br /> <br /> I believe Garou can identify the killers by interrogating spirits that may have witnessed the slaughter,<br /> even if the spirits can't point them towards the killers, they can just tell them &quot;some vampires did it&quot;, and already the coterie is in danger","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-08-2020, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:14:51-07:00","id":1401731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401681#post1401681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gurahl knows a Ritual which can revive the dead but could also ends his life (more details in Gurahl sourcebook or old Werewolf Players Guide).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well,<br /> 1. Rite of Fighting the Death Bear may only raise dead gurahl<br /> <br /> 2. It has details in at least three books: old Players Guide, Gurahl book and W20 Changing Breed<br /> <br /> 3. You don\u2019t need to sacrifice yourself if you defeat Death Bear, although it\u2019s not easy. Specific stats of Death Bear is never provided:<br /> Players Guide doesn\u2019t mention it, it only says in ancient time gurahl only needed to bury dead and waited him to revive, but now the old way collapsed, you need to defeat Death Bear to raise them<br /> Gurahl says it has 10 Willpower, 10 Rage and 10 Gnosis AT LEAST<br /> Changing Breeds says mid-rank gurahl used to defeat him in rare occasions<br /> <br /> But if you\u2019re killed in battle, yeah, you will replace the dead you wanted to raise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-08-2020, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:31:53-07:00","id":1401734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401725#post1401725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP said &quot;they can't move - they're here on Sire's orders&quot;, and they're outside the city,<br /> meaning this coterie is probably the first vampires those garou are gonna meet, and this won't end well for the coterie, even if the garou don't know they're the killers,</div> </div> </div> </div>For months? Again, not knowing the specifics for how long the PCs are supposed to be &quot;there&quot;, what exactly &quot;there&quot; is, why the Sire has told them to stay there, where the Garou are, and how long it will be before they run into the remains of their kinfolk, it seems to me that if it could be months before Garou stumble upon dead kinfolk, then the ST has plenty of wiggle room to let the PCs survive.<br /> <br /> Also, the PCs can disobey their Sire's orders and leave if they're given reason to think its more dangerous for them to remain. What can the sire do that is worse than wiping out the entire coterie? Unless can't disobey Sire is code for &quot;ST mandated plot railroaded and I won't let the PCs do anything I don't want them to do&quot;. In which case, my recommendation is for the ST to allow the game to go off the railroad so the PCs aren't forced to remain in an area to be destroyed simply because the ST didn't bother to think things through beforehand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401725#post1401725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Garou can identify the killers by interrogating spirits that may have witnessed the slaughter,<br /> even if the spirits can't point them towards the killers, they can just tell them &quot;some vampires did it&quot;, and already the coterie is in danger</div> </div> </div> </div>Every ST is different, but I would not rule that except in extraordinary circumstances. The Penumbra is separate from the Realm. Creatures inside one do not normally see what is happening on the other side unless they use certain abilities. So unless the spirits just happened to be Peeking at that exact time, or were using some special Charm that informs them of details of what was happening, the spirits should not be able to tell the Garou anything because they were not witnesses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:45:13-07:00","id":1401737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401734#post1401734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Penumbra is separate from the Realm. Creatures inside one do not normally see what is happening on the other side unless they use certain abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>in VtM, you can talk to spirits of inanimate objects and plants (thaumaturgy - elemental mastery, green path) for investigating<br /> <br /> I'm no expert on WtA, I assumed Garou had such abilities as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:13:03-07:00","id":1401761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401715#post1401715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Garou don't know that these kinfolk are dead, and may not learn until months later, how exactly will they track down their killers? Scent doesn't last that long. And even most supernatural powers won't help you. How will they be able to determine it was the PCs who did this?</div> </div> </div> </div> Apart of interrogating the spirits (as Pleiades said) one camp of Gets have a Gift which help them track the offenders (from W:tA Players Guide, I can't recall the name and don't have my copy right now). And if they have a Corax (wereraven) ally it will be even easier. Also, if the ST allows it the animals living nearby could also help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:23:54-07:00","id":1401764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401731#post1401731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well,<br /> 1. Rite of Fighting the Death Bear may only raise dead gurahl<br /> <br /> 2. It has details in at least three books: old Players Guide, Gurahl book and W20 Changing Breed<br /> <br /> 3. You don\u2019t need to sacrifice yourself if you defeat Death Bear, although it\u2019s not easy. Specific stats of Death Bear is never provided:<br /> Players Guide doesn\u2019t mention it, it only says in ancient time gurahl only needed to bury dead and waited him to revive, but now the old way collapsed, you need to defeat Death Bear to raise them<br /> Gurahl says it has 10 Willpower, 10 Rage and 10 Gnosis AT LEAST<br /> Changing Breeds says mid-rank gurahl used to defeat him in rare occasions<br /> <br /> But if you\u2019re killed in battle, yeah, you will replace the dead you wanted to raise</div> </div> </div> </div>1. As far as I know it works for any recently deceased. The Gurahl denial when Garou demanded that they teach them this Rite was one of the ignition points of War of Rage. I believe that Gurahl simply didn't want to teach them. If it was useless I think that Garou would understand that. And in that case the Gurahl will get a certain advantage: they will get more chances of ressurection their dead. Besides, IMHO, creative Storyteller would allow that.<br /> 2. OK, I don't know W20 Changing Breeds.<br /> 3. I didn't say sacrifice, only risk his life for strangers. I know how this rite works. The &quot;stats&quot; of Death Bear (as you said they weren't published, only suggested) are Rage 10, Gnosis 10, Willpower 10 and Power 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:24:51-07:00","id":1401765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401737#post1401737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> in VtM, you can talk to spirits of inanimate objects and plants (thaumaturgy - elemental mastery, green path) for investigating<br /> <br /> I'm no expert on WtA, I assumed Garou had such abilities as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. They can talk with Spirits and animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:32:33-07:00","id":1401769,"title":"","content":"Give them a fighting chance. Give them a day to prepare for the retaliation and access to silver weapons and the ability to make traps like Conan the Barbarian.<br /> <br /> They can also run.<br /> <br /> Also, let them know the dice will fall where they may. If it works well, you can have the Battle of the Mounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RoZzVUPqHbk\" data-code=\"RoZzVUPqHbk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/RoZzVUPqHbk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:32:38-07:00","id":1401770,"title":"","content":"I got an idea for a twist of plot. Imagine Garou attacking coterie and suddenly someone/something helps the characters: throwing objects at them, igniting fires. It is one of the Kinfolk who ended as a Restless Dead and certainly won't allow ANYONE take his revenge from him (his main passion). Of course they will have to deal with the angry Wraith but an able Thaumaturgist or Giovanni/Samedi could easily deal with it... for a price of course. He could also become a Risen (which means pacting with his Shadow) and is overrun with Shade powers. That could lead to an &quot;alliance&quot; between Garou and coterie (the first ones want to stop the Kinfolk as he is now outside Gaia's circle, the coterie just want to survive). Of course there's just one small problem: what will happen after \ud83d\ude08.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-08-2020, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:06:16-07:00","id":1401781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401765#post1401765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More or less. They can talk with Spirits and animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering about those spirits of inanimate objects and plants,<br /> are they from our side of the gauntlet or are they still on the other side?<br /> <br /> their description in VtM makes it sound like they're on our side<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T20:03:16-07:00","id":1401835,"title":"","content":"So, I don't know enough about D20, so this might be a bit different there.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd say a lot of things depend on how long the PCs stick around, who exactly the werewolves are, how organized the local werewolves are, and how stupid/suicidal the player characters are.<br /> <br /> So, what tribes of werewolves live in the area? If they're Silent Striders, then the characters are probably going to die. They almost certainly have someone who can do the proper rite (Descent Into the Underworld in main WtA) to transfer over into the Underworld and just straight up ask the kinfolk's ghosts who killed them. &quot;I was murdered by vampires before I could warn my werewolf kin&quot; is definitely some very valid &quot;unfinished business&quot;.<br /> <br /> If they're someone a little less mystically canny, the characters might have a little time. All tribes probably have someone on hand who can talk to spirits, but spirits aren't all-seeing and all-knowing either. Other mystically in-tune tribes like Uktena and Wendigo have likely set spirits to watch their kinfolk, but others may or may not be more reactive and take longer to figure out the kinfolk are dead. Depends on how far ranging the local packs are and who exactly is checking in on kinfolk.<br /> <br /> If/when the werewolves figure out what the situation is and that it was vampires, this is likely a TPK. Werewolves aren't stupid and know enough about vampires to attack at a time to their advantage - as you say, during the day they're basically just corpses waiting for the sun. If the coterie is stupid enough to hang around where they murdered a family of kinfollk, and they know who they killed... yeah, &quot;My sire told me to stay here so I'm staying here!&quot; shouldn't be their response. Even if they're all full blood-bonded, at least one of them should be making the rationalization of &quot;... but I'm also pretty sure my sire probably wants me to live&quot; at this point. If not... TPK.<br /> <br /> One thing that could happen is a local vampire, likely a Gangrel, showing up mad and demanding that the coterie move off before the werewolves just straight up murder everyone. This might give them some motivation to depart and make it clear to them that this isn't a &quot;but my sire said!&quot; sort of moment.<br /> <br /> If that fails, give the characters a chance to roll some &quot;this is suicidally stupid&quot; checks. If THAT fails, give the players an OOC &quot;this is suicidally stupid&quot; talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 07-08-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T20:04:56-07:00","id":1401836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401781#post1401781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm wondering about those spirits of inanimate objects and plants,<br /> are they from our side of the gauntlet or are they still on the other side?<br /> <br /> their description in VtM makes it sound like they're on our side</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't really matter for almost any sort of inanimate object or plant type spirit. Most location based spirits have the &quot;Realm-Sense&quot; ability, which lets them sense what's going on in both the Umbra and real world locations they're bound to. They need to make a roll, but it's a pretty easy one for most spirits that have this power. That's the spirit a decent Theurge would be asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 07-08-2020, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T13:50:36-07:00","id":1401958,"title":"","content":"Some things I'm surprised people have missed.<br /> <br /> An impressive body of water (Lake, Raging river, Sea) is an excellent escape from lupines: The local garou are unlikely to have &quot;spirit of the fish&quot; and probably don't have the sensory powers for dark and murky waters. Sure, the players will end up leaving their retinue at the mercy of enraged lupines, but the players can probably survive this way. <br /> <br /> If possible, the players could take the remaining kinfolk hostage.<br /> <br /> The players might stand a fighting chance if they Ghouled <i>all </i>or most of their retinue. A defensive formation of 15 ghouls and a combat monster vampire should be able to hold off three or four fosterns assuming these people are reasonably competent. Perhaps your other players can use this defence to try their own tricks. <br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to laugh at the players; They find a silver mine, one of the NPC party members develops true faith and prays away the lupines, one of the party knows some hearth lore and recognizes some plants to keep the lupines away....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T17:13:43-07:00","id":1401990,"title":"","content":"To be honest, this sounds a bit like the ST maneuvered them into it. The kinfolk found _them_, and there was, apparently, no option of wiping their memory from what OP wrote, and the setup is that they can't leave the place where they're surely going to be found, can't really set up a defence, can't call in allies... they can't really do much of anything.<br /> <br /> It might sound silly, but what if, once the Garou find their kinfolk murdered, they go off, howling for revenge... in the wrong direction? And murder whatever leeches they find there? In fact, the Garou might go into the nearest city for it, because what leech is dumb enough to actually _stay_ out in the countryside after painting a huge target on their backs? Then the vampires strike back, more werewolves get involved, and things escalate. Essentially, the coterie kicked off a nice little local supernatural war, and they better hope to Caine nobody traces it back to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T18:21:48-07:00","id":1401999,"title":"","content":"Deja vu all over again.<br /> <br /> Seriously,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice\"> this other thread was pretty recent</a>. Very recent. I have soy milk in my fridge I bought before that thread started. It's still in date.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice/page3\">Go here. Read this.</a> No seriously, I just wrote an opinion on almost exactly this same question less than two months ago. The specifics of the poster's question were slightly different, and yet eerily similar.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: Do not introduce a story element you are not prepared to deal with. If you do, get rid of that element as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> Options: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They weren't really kinfolk. They were lying to save themselves from the vampires.</li> <li>The garou are really bad at their job and never find the pcs.</li> <li>The sire who sent them here sends them somewhere else. I hear Montevideo is nice.</li> <li>A deus ex machina wipes out the pack. Plane crashes into the pack's house?</li> <li>Give the pcs new friends. Pentex will help them out!</li> <li>The garou show up and the pcs convince them someone else did it. Blame it on Nephandi.</li> <li>It was all a psychic vision of how gehenna will start. Then the pcs woke up, and meet the kinfolk again for the first time.</li> <li>Have the players make up new characters investigating the disappearance of the current pcs. Play the current pcs and the new pcs in parallel, a year apart. Points for being super-artsy!</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T18:56:03-07:00","id":1402002,"title":"","content":"In the unlikely scenario that the actual pack manages to figure out who killed the family, the coterie is screwed unless the decide &quot;fuck this&quot; and bail to a city. Mithras, who is millenia older than this coterie (assuming here), has a metric fuckload invested in Fortitude and combat experience, barely managed to defeat 2 packs. And he was ripped to shit and barely conscious in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> If, by some chance, the pack manages to track them down in the wild, they will be hard pressed to get away unscathed. Garou have vampires in general under &quot;kill on sight&quot; mentality, unless they are Black Spiral Dancers, as vampires are walking wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> The only way out of this diplomatically is if the coterie takes the lead and manages to get 1 shifter away from the pack and hope like hell they can talk it down and run when talks inevitably fall apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T23:31:40-07:00","id":1402017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401781#post1401781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering about those spirits of inanimate objects and plants,<br /> are they from our side of the gauntlet or are they still on the other side?<br /> <br /> their description in VtM makes it sound like they're on our side</div> </div> </div> </div>All spirits are in the Penumbra on the other side of the Gauntlet unless they specifically happen to Materialize in the Realm. Spirits present in the Realm are always the exception, never the rule. (Normally in Vampire which does not usually deal with spirit things, I would not nitpick and simply let the ST do whatever they want. But if the ST asks how it is &quot;supposed&quot; to operate, I'm going to tell her that.)<br /> <br /> And most inanimate objects and plants do not have spirits that are currently awake. They are usually in slumber, and a Garou would need to first wake them up with the Rite of Spirit Awakening. Needless to say, if the spirit was in slumber during that time, they have can have no knowledge of what happened regardless of what powers they have.<br /> <br /> And while the Charm Realm Sense can allow some spirits to sense what transpires in its domain in the Realm, it is a power that must be actively used. It is just a way to allow spirits to remotely do Peeking instead of being directly there. In other words, unless the spirit was using that power at the time these events occurred, it won't know what was happening. The most they can do is use it now and have access to the exact same information the Garou would when they stumble across it later. They can't use it to time travel back to the past and see what happened. They would need some sort of postcognitive ability, and that is not a standard power.<br /> <br /> The ST can arrange all sorts of things in order to have a spirit present and using its powers to sense the place at that exact time. It's not the most likely coincidence at any random place, but it could happen. But since the ST is looking for ways to give the PCs an out, why would he want to rule that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:25:02-07:00","id":1402047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401958#post1401958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things I'm surprised people have missed.<br /> <br /> An impressive body of water (Lake, Raging river, Sea) is an excellent escape from lupines: The local garou are unlikely to have &quot;spirit of the fish&quot; and probably don't have the sensory powers for dark and murky waters. Sure, the players will end up leaving their retinue at the mercy of enraged lupines, but the players can probably survive this way. <br /> <br /> If possible, the players could take the remaining kinfolk hostage.<br /> <br /> The players might stand a fighting chance if they Ghouled <i>all </i>or most of their retinue. A defensive formation of 15 ghouls and a combat monster vampire should be able to hold off three or four fosterns assuming these people are reasonably competent. Perhaps your other players can use this defence to try their own tricks. <br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to laugh at the players; They find a silver mine, one of the NPC party members develops true faith and prays away the lupines, one of the party knows some hearth lore and recognizes some plants to keep the lupines away....</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that they were missed. Rather ommited deliberately. Remember, it was a ST who wants to to know what he can do about it not the players. The idea of walking through the lake is nice but that is a thing that players should invent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-10-2020, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:32:56-07:00","id":1402048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401999#post1401999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deja vu all over again.<br /> <br /> Seriously,<a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice&quot;]</a> this other thread was pretty recent[/URL]. Very recent. I have soy milk in my fridge I bought before that thread started. It's still in date.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice/page3&quot;]Go</a> here. Read this.[/URL] No seriously, I just wrote an opinion on almost exactly this same question less than two months ago. The specifics of the poster's question were slightly different, and yet eerily similar.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: Do not introduce a story element you are not prepared to deal with. If you do, get rid of that element as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> Options:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They weren't really kinfolk. They were lying to save themselves from the vampires.</li> <li>The garou are really bad at their job and never find the pcs.</li> <li>The sire who sent them here sends them somewhere else. I hear Montevideo is nice.</li> <li>A deus ex machina wipes out the pack. Plane crashes into the pack's house?</li> <li>Give the pcs new friends. Pentex will help them out!</li> <li>The garou show up and the pcs convince them someone else did it. Blame it on Nephandi.</li> <li>It was all a psychic vision of how gehenna will start. Then the pcs woke up, and meet the kinfolk again for the first time.</li> <li>Have the players make up new characters investigating the disappearance of the current pcs. Play the current pcs and the new pcs in parallel, a year apart. Points for being super-artsy!</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. How do they know what Kinfolk is?<br /> 2. Rite of the Questing Stone works pretty good. Ok, without the names it would be harder but still possible.<br /> 3. It works as long as the sept on which protectorate PCs will hide is at war with the sept of the pack who chase PCs. If not they will rather help the pack avenge their relatives. It's a duty of all Garou to avenge the Kinfolks. <br /> 4. Highly unlikely but still one of the most realistic IMHO.<br /> 5. This will work only if Pentex knows more than the pack.<br /> 6. As with 1. <br /> 7. Ok, this one's nice.<br /> 8. Nice, but not every player want to create a new character apart of the difficulty playing 2 characters at one time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-10-2020, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:39:44-07:00","id":1402049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1401990#post1401990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, this sounds a bit like the ST maneuvered them into it. The kinfolk found _them_, and there was, apparently, no option of wiping their memory from what OP wrote, and the setup is that they can't leave the place where they're surely going to be found, can't really set up a defence, can't call in allies... they can't really do much of anything.<br /> <br /> It might sound silly, but what if, once the Garou find their kinfolk murdered, they go off, howling for revenge... in the wrong direction? And murder whatever leeches they find there? In fact, the Garou might go into the nearest city for it, because what leech is dumb enough to actually _stay_ out in the countryside after painting a huge target on their backs? Then the vampires strike back, more werewolves get involved, and things escalate. Essentially, the coterie kicked off a nice little local supernatural war, and they better hope to Caine nobody traces it back to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that one's good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:42:39-07:00","id":1402052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1402047#post1402047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that they were missed. Rather ommited deliberately. Remember, it was a ST who wants to to know what he can do about it not the players. The idea of walking through the lake is nice but that is a thing that players should invent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The players can't hide in the a lake if the storyteller doesn't give them one. The storyteller should guide the game towards giving players good potential options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:45:49-07:00","id":1402053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1402002#post1402002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the unlikely scenario that the actual pack manages to figure out who killed the family, the coterie is screwed unless the decide &quot;fuck this&quot; and bail to a city. Mithras, who is millenia older than this coterie (assuming here), has a metric fuckload invested in Fortitude and combat experience, barely managed to defeat 2 packs. And he was ripped to shit and barely conscious in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> If, by some chance, the pack manages to track them down in the wild, they will be hard pressed to get away unscathed. Garou have vampires in general under &quot;kill on sight&quot; mentality, unless they are Black Spiral Dancers, as vampires are walking wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> The only way out of this diplomatically is if the coterie takes the lead and manages to get 1 shifter away from the pack and hope like hell they can talk it down and run when talks inevitably fall apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also end Rambo style: the characters have some time to set traps and defend themselves against the pack. It's not so hard as you think. Once my lone Gangrel (combat oriented, with none of combat abilities above 3, Fortitude 3 and Celerity 1 and .38 Special without silver bullets, XIII Gen) manage to kill 2 and chase away 3 Garou, and, during the same night, kill 6 and stake 3 Sabat vampires letting their ghoul escape to carry the warning. It non combat mortal who defeated 8 Generation combat oriented Gangrel (this time he staked himself, he botches the attack roll very bad and the fight was in the woods so my ST assumed that). And, cause my ST was a dice roller it was all fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:49:28-07:00","id":1402054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1402052#post1402052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The players can't hide in the a lake if the storyteller doesn't give them one. The storyteller should guide the game towards giving players good potential options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, explanation accepted \ud83d\ude09.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T16:32:19-07:00","id":1402141,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2337\" data-vbnamecard=\"2337\">Quatar</a> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that you are running a VtM game. &quot;Garou&quot;, as described in Werewolf: the Apocalypse, do not exist. Creatures the vampires call &quot;Lupines&quot; exist.<br /> <br /> Here's my advice: stop reading the werewolf book, and create the creatures you need for your game! An adolescent werewolf has Celerity 3, Potence 1, and Protean 4. That's a Lupine, and a reasonable match for most pcs. (see V20, page 378)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T02:47:26-07:00","id":1402208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1402141#post1402141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2337\" data-vbnamecard=\"2337\">Quatar</a> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that you are running a VtM game. &quot;Garou&quot;, as described in Werewolf: the Apocalypse, do not exist. Creatures the vampires call &quot;Lupines&quot; exist.<br /> <br /> Here's my advice: stop reading the werewolf book, and create the creatures you need for your game! An adolescent werewolf has Celerity 3, Potence 1, and Protean 4. That's a Lupine, and a reasonable match for most pcs. (see V20, page 378)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. But there was also the word Kinfolk which points that they are Garou. The author used also the word werewolves, not Lupines. So I think it can be assumed that he's looking for advices about how to deal with the situation with Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T04:46:26-07:00","id":1402224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1402208#post1402208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok. But there was also the word Kinfolk which points that they are Garou. The author used also the word werewolves, not Lupines. So I think it can be assumed that he's looking for advices about how to deal with the situation with Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main problem we're trying to solve is that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2337\" data-vbnamecard=\"2337\">Quatar</a> is running Garou (people who become wolves and kill vampires, the term itself is irrelevant) using Werewolf corebook rules.<br /> <br /> This is for a V20 Vampire the Masquerade game, right? It seems reasonable to suggest Quatar use the VtM corebook rules, while putting WtA back on the shelf.<br /> <br /> In V20, pp378-379, there is a write-up for creatures called &quot;Werewolves&quot; or &quot;Lupines&quot;. This write-up has already been balanced to make lupines dangerous adversaries for vampires, but not walking woodchippers with infinite backup of more lupines to call in if they fail. There is nothing in V20 which says or implies that &quot;kinfolk&quot; don't exist. They can take human form, so presumably they have relations with humans, thus creating kinfolk.<br /> <br /> This is one happy instance in which using the corebook, canon, raw rules fixes the problem.<br /> <br /> Well done, corebook writers and developers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T01:23:32-07:00","id":1402381,"title":"","content":"I think the VTM rules for werewolves are shallow (on purpose) and in a game with lots of rural activity, a richer, WTA werewolf is warranted. <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, one first edition rule worth adding to even things out a bit:<br /> Vampires can soak Claws and fangs with their stamina, the damage is aggravated, but that only matters in terms of healing. (of course if your players have like 2 stamina this ain't gonna matter much) <br /> This balances fights a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T20:40:04-07:00","id":1402726,"title":"","content":"It was that way in 2nd Edition as well. Werewolves were still dangerous and tended to have a significant advantage in physical prowess over neonate vampires one-on-one, but they weren't effortlessly shredding elders before they could blink in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T02:29:31-07:00","id":1402769,"title":"","content":"The players can easily beat this problem with deception. It doesn\u2019t matter that the werewolves can overpower them if they are tricked. <br /> <br /> The players can falsify evidence. Make false witnesses. Etc. <br /> <br /> Garou who find obvious \u201canswers\u201d shouldn\u2019t need to utilize magical investigation means if they have a target for revenge already. <br /> <br /> Direct them to the coteries enemies. Every vampire makes enemies given enough time. There is no reason deception couldn\u2019t beat this encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:56:15-07:00","id":1402848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401635-d20-how-to-use-lupines-as-a-threat-but-not-entirely-wipe-the-coterie?p=1402224#post1402224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main problem we're trying to solve is that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2337\" data-vbnamecard=\"2337\">Quatar</a> is running Garou (people who become wolves and kill vampires, the term itself is irrelevant) using Werewolf corebook rules.<br /> <br /> This is for a V20 Vampire the Masquerade game, right? It seems reasonable to suggest Quatar use the VtM corebook rules, while putting WtA back on the shelf.<br /> <br /> In V20, pp378-379, there is a write-up for creatures called &quot;Werewolves&quot; or &quot;Lupines&quot;. This write-up has already been balanced to make lupines dangerous adversaries for vampires, but not walking woodchippers with infinite backup of more lupines to call in if they fail. There is nothing in V20 which says or implies that &quot;kinfolk&quot; don't exist. They can take human form, so presumably they have relations with humans, thus creating kinfolk.<br /> <br /> This is one happy instance in which using the corebook, canon, raw rules fixes the problem.<br /> <br /> Well done, corebook writers and developers!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have avoided posting in this thread since I don't use the other game lines, but I think this is a spot on way to run Werewolves. They just aren't the stars of a vampire game, the vampires are. I don't find the games cross over well in practice, other than the Mummy supplement that was built to work with VTM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}